+# OWASP Top 10 for LLM Apps (2025) — control-vs-gap mapping for this fleet
+
+**Lane:** R29 (scout radar VIII, `docs/SCOUT_RADAR_2026-10-28-VIII.md`) · **Issue:** #1733 · **Probed:** 2026-10-28 against main `0b19b36` (every file path below was opened and read; nothing is cited from memory).
+**Taxonomy version pin:** OWASP **Top 10 for LLM Apps & GenAI Apps — 2025** (v2025 published 2024-11; official translations through 2025-07; license **CC BY-SA 4.0**). OWASP text is **paraphrased, never copied**; category names are short identifiers used for navigation.
+**Re-base trigger (pre-registered):** the OWASP GitHub mirror marked the 2025 repository "legacy" on **2026-08-05** and points to a 2026 release in flight. When the 2026 list is published, a follow-up lane must re-base this table row-by-row and diff the category set; until then this document pins 2025 and says so on every use.
+
+> **This document is not a control.** A mapping is evidence for humans about where controls live; it blocks nothing, enforces nothing, and must never be cited as if it did. Every enforcement claim below names the file that actually enforces. The companion never-do rule from #1733 applies: no modification of the guard chain happened to produce this file (docs-only, zero source changes, zero dependencies, `.github/` untouched).
+
+## Reading the verdicts
+
+- **ENFORCED** — the named file/tool sits on main and runs as a standing gate (guard roster `scripts/ci/run_all_guards.py`, CI job, pre-push hook, or a wired request-path module in `infrastructure/mcp-control-plane/src/`).
+- **PARTIAL** — a real control exists but is bounded: ad-hoc (not rostered), inventory-only, best-effort, or covers a subset of the category.
+- **GAP** — no control found on main for that slice of the category. Gap cells are the actionable half of this document.
+
